# End-to-end EMULATOR test for the BIGTREETECH SKR mini E3 v2.0
# (STM32F103) in DETERMINISTIC TICK MODE. Boots klipper firmware under
# Renode against the skr-mini-e3-v2.0 pin map, completes klippy
# identify + clocksync, brings up the full MCU config (4 TMC2209s, 2
# software-PWM heaters, 2 fans, endstops, 2 thermistors), reads the
# thermistors through ADC1, round-trips the four TMC2209 register files
# over the shared software UART, and exercises interactive gcode
# (M114/M105) against real firmware.
#
# This is the STM32 sibling of duet2_maestro.test (SAM4S). The new
# ground it covers vs that template:
#
#   - TMC2209 MULTI-DROP UART addressing: all four drivers share one
#     software-UART bus (PC11 rx / PC10 tx) and are distinguished by
#     uart_address (0/2/1/3) in the datagram, not by a select-pin mux.
#     The reply is always master-addressed (sync=0x05, addr=0xff) per
#     the TMC datasheet, so renode_hooks.sw_uart serves every address
#     from one shared register file; klippy's per-driver IFCNT
#     write-verify still lines up because it initialises the drivers
#     sequentially. DUMP_TMC below reads back the live register file
#     for the addr-0 (stepper_x) and addr-3 (extruder) drivers, proving
#     the UART read path works at both ends of the address range.
#   - Plain (non-adc_scaled) thermistors on ADC1 channel 0 (PA0,
#     extruder) and channel 13 (PC3, bed), read end to end by M105 via
#     test/emulator/stm32_adc_stub.py - a Python.PythonPeripheral that
#     completes klipper's F1 SWSTART -> STRT/EOC -> SQR3/DR ADC handshake
#     (upstream Renode's Analog.STM32_ADC does not, so without the stub
#     every heater reads a flat temp=0.0). The fixture feeds both ~34 C.
#
# As with duet2_maestro, the gated path is MOTION-FREE: tick-mode
# resolves the renode wall-clock-vs-virtual-time drift, but motion
# commands (homing) are delivered by klippy's wall-clock-paced
# serialqueue background thread, which under shared-host CPU contention
# can deliver a tightly-scheduled stepper command late and trip "Timer
# too close" (the same serialqueue/sim-time issue that keeps the
# renode-tick-homing tests out of the default CMD). The boot / config /
# TMC-init / ADC / DUMP_TMC / M114 / M105 path schedules no such
# tight-lead commands and is deterministically green. The firmware is
# the generic serial-mode stm32f103 build (stm32f103.dict); the real
# board is USB-only but the STM32F103 Renode platform models no USB
# device, and the printer pin map this test exercises is independent of
# the host link.
DICTIONARY stm32f103.dict
CONFIG skr_mini_e3_v2.cfg
EMULATOR skr_mini_e3_v2.fixture.json
REQUIRES_EMULATOR  # deterministic-time lockstep needs the real backend

# Interactive gcode round-trip against real firmware in tick mode.
# M114 reports toolhead position; M105 reports temperatures, reading
# both thermistors through ADC1 end to end. Neither drives a stepper.
M114
M105
# Read back the live TMC register file over the multi-drop UART for the
# lowest and highest addressed drivers. DUMP_TMC reads every register
# (incl. IOIN) live, so it only produces a full dump if the firmware
# round-tripped the read datagrams for that driver's address.
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=stepper_x
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=extruder

# klippy connected, loaded the dictionary, and built the full config
# against real firmware.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Configured MCU 'mcu'"
# DUMP_TMC dumped both ends of the address range (addr 0 / addr 3); the
# IOIN read returning the TMC2209 version byte (0x21) proves the
# multi-drop UART read path returned framed, CRC-valid responses.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC stepper_x"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC extruder"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "version=0x21"
# A broken UART round-trip surfaces as a TMC init failure or a direct
# read/write error; the deterministic tick clock must produce neither.
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to read tmc uart"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to write tmc uart"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
# A renode-side crash (wrong sysbus peripheral, hook callback error)
# kills serial; klippy then gets EOF and TMC init / identify time out.
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Got EOF when reading from device"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init: Timeout"
# With the deterministic clock the config / TMC / ADC path pushes no
# deadline into the firmware's past, so nothing shuts down.
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "ADC out of range"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Timer too close"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Rescheduled timer in the past"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
